.TH DIPIREC 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipirec \- record or replay a DVB-IPI stream to a file, multicast, or an RTMP(S) server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipirec
.B \-i
.I <uri>
.B \-o
.I <target>
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipirec
records a DVB-IPI transport stream to a file, stdout, multicast, a RIST
or SRT peer, or an RTMP(S) ingest server. Output
.RB ( \-o )
is repeatable, up to 8 targets, so several destinations can be fed from
a single source at once. With
.B \-\-pace
a file or stdin source is replayed at its own original timing instead
of being read as fast as possible.
.PP
Sources accepted by
.B \-i
are:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B rtp://@<group>:<port>
\- RTP wrapped SPTS multicast (the \fB@\fR is optional)
.IP \(bu 2
.B udp://@<group>:<port>
\- raw SPTS multicast (the \fB@\fR is optional)
.IP \(bu 2
.B http://<host>:<port>/<path>
or
.B https://<host>:<port>/<path>
\- an HTTP(S) TS stream (\fB\-\-insecure\fR skips TLS verification on
\fBhttps://\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
.B \-
\- stdin, plain TS or RTP-wrapped TS, auto-detected
.IP \(bu 2
.I <path>
\- a file, plain TS or RTP-wrapped TS, auto-detected
.IP \(bu 2
.B rist://@<host>:<port>[?query]
\- single-peer RIST receiver (\fB@\fR required, marks it as listening;
requires librist; no bonding here, use
.BR dipirist (1)
as a bridge for that)
.IP \(bu 2
.B srt://[@]<host>:<port>
\- single-peer SRT receiver (\fB@\fR binds/listens/accepts, else calls
out; requires libsrt; no bonding or rendezvous here, use
.BR dipisrt (1)
as a bridge for those)
.IP \(bu 2
IPv6 groups are given in brackets, e.g.
.B rtp://@[ff3e::1]:8700
.RE
.PP
Output targets accepted by
.B \-o
are a plain file path or
.B \-
for stdout, plus:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B rtp://@<group>:<port>
\- RTP-wrapped multicast (\fB\-f raw\fR or \fB\-f ts\fR only)
.IP \(bu 2
.B udp://@<group>:<port>
\- raw multicast, no RTP header (\fB\-f raw\fR or \fB\-f ts\fR only)
.IP \(bu 2
.B rist://<host>:<port>[?query]
\- single-peer RIST sender (\fB\-f raw\fR or \fB\-f ts\fR only, requires
librist)
.IP \(bu 2
.B srt://<host>:<port>
\- single-peer SRT sender (\fB\-f raw\fR or \fB\-f ts\fR only, requires
libsrt, always calls out - no listener mode). Independent per target, not
bonded - repeat \fB\-o\fR for more, or use
.BR dipisrt (1)
if you need bonded peers
.IP \(bu 2
.B rtmp(s)://<host>[:port]/<app>/<key>
\- RTMP(S) publish; H.264/HEVC video, AC-3/E-AC-3/AAC audio
.RE
.PP
The
.B \-f
option selects the recording format: \fBraw\fR (RTP unwrapped only,
transport stream otherwise untouched), \fBts\fR (single program transport
stream, drops stuffing/NIT/EIT/AIT/CA-EMM, keeps SDT, rewrites PAT/PMT),
.B mkv
(Matroska with H.264/HEVC video and AC3/EAC3/MP2/MP3/AAC/AAC-LATM audio) or
.B mka
(Matroska, audio only). Without \fB\-f\fR the format is taken from the
.B \-o
file suffix, defaulting to \fBts\fR.
.PP
.B mkv
and
.B mka
containers and \fBsrt\fR subtitles decoded from EBU Teletext are additions
beyond the DVB-IPI specification, as is the HTTP(S) source.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out\ \fI<target>\fR
Output, repeatable: a file, \fB\-\fR for stdout, or an
\fBrtp://\fR/\fBudp://\fR/\fBrist://\fR/\fBsrt://\fR/\fBrtmp://\fR/\fBrtmps://\fR
target (see DESCRIPTION).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-in\ \fI<uri>\fR
Input source (see DESCRIPTION).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-audio\ \fI<track>\fR
Audio track, numbered from 1, or \fBall\fR. Default: \fBall\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format\ \fI<format>\fR
.IR raw | ts | mkv | mka .
Default: taken from the
.B \-o
suffix, else \fBts\fR.
.B mkv
and
.B mka
are rejected together with a network
.B \-o
target; \fBraw\fR is rejected alongside any \fB\-o rtmp://\fR or
\fB\-o rtmps://\fR target.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pmt\-pid\ \fI<pid>\fR | \fIall\fR
MPTS source only: pin one program's PMT pid, or record every program
(\fBall\fR; rejected with \fB\-f mkv\fR). Ignored, with a warning, on an
SPTS source. If omitted on an MPTS source the tool fails early and lists
the available programs.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-subtitles\ \fI<mode>\fR
.IR strip | keep | srt .
.B srt
is valid only with \fBmkv\fR/\fBmka\fR. Default: \fBkeep\fR.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time\ \fI<duration>\fR
Recording duration, e.g. \fB90\fR, \fB5m\fR, \fB5m30s\fR, \fB1h3m20s\fR,
\fB01:20:03\fR, \fB10:20\fR. Without \fB\-t\fR the recording runs until
stopped.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface\ \fI<iface>\fR
Interface for
.BR \-i 's
multicast join.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-out\-iface\ \fI<iface>\fR
Interface for
.BR \-o
\fBrtp://\fR/\fBudp://\fR's multicast send.
.TP
.B \-\-ttl \fI<n>\fR
Multicast TTL / hop limit for
.B \-o
\fBrtp://\fR/\fBudp://\fR. Default: kernel default (1).
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fI<p>\fR
.IR simple | main .
.B \-o
.B rist://
only. Default: \fBsimple\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-secret \fI<psk>\fR
.B \-o
.B rist://
pre-shared key; requires \fB\-\-profile main\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-cname \fI<name>\fR
.B \-o
.B rist://
cname. Default: library default.
.TP
.B \-\-buffer \fI<ms>\fR
.B \-o
.B rist://
recovery buffer. Default: library default.
.TP
.B \-\-profile\-in \fI<p>\fR
.IR simple | main .
.B \-i
.B rist://
only. Default: \fBsimple\fR. \fBmain\fR enables PSK encryption via a
.B ?secret=
query parameter on the input URI.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-passphrase\-in \fI<pw>\fR
Passphrase for
.B \-i
.B srt://
only, 10..79 characters. Default: none (no encryption).
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-pbkeylen\-in \fI16\fR|\fI24\fR|\fI32\fR
AES key length, requires
.BR \-\-srt\-passphrase\-in .
Default: 16.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-streamid\-in \fI<id>\fR
SRTO_STREAMID for
.B \-i
.B srt://
only.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-packetfilter\-in \fI<cfg>\fR
SRTO_PACKETFILTER config string for
.B \-i
.B srt://
only, e.g.
.IR fec,cols:10,rows:5 .
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-latency\-in \fI<ms>\fR
SRTO_LATENCY for
.B \-i
.B srt://
only. Default: library.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-passphrase \fI<pw>\fR
Passphrase applied to every
.B \-o
.B srt://
target, 10..79 characters. Default: none (no encryption).
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-pbkeylen \fI16\fR|\fI24\fR|\fI32\fR
AES key length, requires
.BR \-\-srt\-passphrase .
Default: 16.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-streamid \fI<id>\fR
SRTO_STREAMID applied to every
.B \-o
.B srt://
target.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-packetfilter \fI<cfg>\fR
SRTO_PACKETFILTER config string applied to every
.B \-o
.B srt://
target.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-latency \fI<ms>\fR
SRTO_LATENCY applied to every
.B \-o
.B srt://
target. Default: library.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate/hostname/expiry verification for
.B \-o
.B rtmps://
and
.B \-i
.BR https:// .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Periodic recording stats on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-sub\-lead \fI<ms>\fR
Shift subtitles earlier. Default: 1000.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fI<path>\fR
Unix datagram socket for metrics. Default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fI<name>\fR
Stable instance id. Metrics stay disabled unless this is set.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fI<s>\fR
Snapshot interval in seconds. Default: 5.
.TP
.B \-\-ret \fI<addr>:<port>\fR
RET server unicast address (\fB\-i rtp://\fR only); enables gap repair.
Its address family must match
.BR \-i 's,
unless
.B \-\-no\-ret\-mc
is also given.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ret\-mc
Skip joining the RET server's multicast repair session.
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-mc\-port \fI<port>\fR
Override the repair session port. Default: \fB\-i\fR's port.
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-pt \fI<n>\fR
RTX payload type, must match the RET server. Default: 99.
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-wait \fI<ms>\fR
Hold budget after a NACK before giving up on a gap. Default: 200.
.TP
.B \-\-pace
File/stdin source only: pace output to the input's own timing (RTP
timestamp if RTP-framed, else PCR).
.TP
.B \-\-strip \fI<list>\fR
.B \-f
.B ts
only: comma list of
.IR NUL , NIT , AIT , EIT , CAT , ECM , EMM , RST , TDT , TOT , INT
to drop, or \fBnone\fR. Default: \fBNUL,NIT,AIT,EIT\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipirec \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-o show.ts
Plain recording to a transport stream file.
.TP
.B dipirec \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-o show.mkv \-s srt \-t 1h30m \-v
Matroska recording with SRT subtitle burn-in, a 90-minute time limit, and
live stats.
.TP
.B dipirec \-i udp://@239.0.175.1:8700 \-o radio.mka \-I eth0
Audio-only Matroska recording, join on a specific interface.
.TP
.B dipirec \-i http://10.0.0.1:4022/rtp/239.19.75.1:8700 \-o show.ts
Recording via an HTTP TS proxy instead of a direct multicast join.
.TP
.B dipirec \-i show.ts \-\-pace \-o rtp://@239.9.9.9:6000 \-O eth1 \-\-ttl 16
Replay a file back onto multicast at its original timing.
.TP
.B dipirec \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-o rtmp://live.example.com/app/key
Relay a multicast source live to an RTMP ingest server.
.TP
.B dipirec \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-o show.ts \-\-ret 10.0.0.1:6000
Record with RET gap repair against a
.BR dipifccret (1)
edge server.
.TP
.B dipirec \-i rtp://@239.1.1.3:5000 \-p all \-o all_channels.mka
MPTS source: every program's audio into one MKA file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B nonzero
Argument error, or I/O failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipiscan (1),
.BR dipisds (1),
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipirist (1),
.BR dipisrt (1),
.BR dipifccret (1)
.PP
